**Bug Fixed:**

The issue was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was accessing `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element) when trying to return the first word.

This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello' 
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.

All tests now pass successfully.
